Loaded 1 tool(s): user_goals. Full interfaces follow; they are callable normally from now on.

## user_goals

Create a goal when the user is working toward an enduring outcome, behavior,
or area of life; after creating it, read the coaching guide linked from the
goal's `GOAL.md`. Recognize durable goals even when the user never says
"goal": repeated aspirations, progress updates, setbacks, commitments with a
timeframe, or asking for help with a whole area of life. Not goals: fleeting
todos, one-time reminders, minor updates that belong on an existing goal.
Clarify one question at a time (an `option` widget suits bounded choices) and
listen for the underlying goal behind the stated one. Coach, don't
task-manage: stay light, raise a goal only when relevant to the current
conversation, and log milestone wins that same turn without derailing the
topic.

Use `list`, `search`, and `view` to resolve goal identity before creating or
updating. `search` matches terms across goal ids, titles, `current_state`,
and descriptions and returns lifecycle state and timestamps.

Every `set_status` call requires a concise user-facing `reason` explaining
the transition.

Each goal has a workspace at `workspace/goals/<goal-slug>/`; read its
`GOAL.md` first before doing anything related to the goal.

### Parameters (JSON Schema)
```json
{
  "additionalProperties": false,
  "properties": {
    "action": {
      "description": "Action to perform. Each action description lists its required and optional sibling arguments.",
      "oneOf": [
        {
          "const": "list",
          "description": "List goals. Optional args: limit."
        },
        {
          "const": "view",
          "description": "View one goal. Required args: goal_id."
        },
        {
          "const": "search",
          "description": "Search this tool's goals across lifecycle states. Required args: query. Optional args: limit."
        },
        {
          "const": "create",
          "description": "Create a goal. Required args: title, current_state, description. Optional args: emoji, parent_goal_id, category, goal_kind, value_alignment."
        },
        {
          "const": "update",
          "description": "Update goal metadata. Required args: goal_id. Optional args: title, current_state, description, parent_goal_id, category, goal_kind, value_alignment, pushable. Use update only for an explicit correction that is not already represented by a new activity entry; do not append a generic next step. Use parent_goal_id to move a goal under a new parent; pass empty string to detach to top-level."
        },
        {
          "const": "delete",
          "description": "Delete a goal. Required args: goal_id."
        },
        {
          "const": "add_entry",
          "description": "Add an activity entry to a goal timeline. Required args: goal_id, title, current_state, description. Optional args: effective_at. For every goal type, the runtime replaces the goal's pulse when the activity supports a newer or more useful current or forward-looking status and otherwise preserves it. Do not make a separate update call solely for the runtime's state decision. For assistant-tracked work, log activity incrementally whenever anything happens, including a step starting or completing, a check, new or confirmed information, deliverable progress, an artifact change, a result, checkpoint, check-in, feedback, direction change, blocker, schedule change, or lifecycle change. Do not wait for a milestone or material change. Keep the entry concise and user-facing, say what happened and any result, and record each activity once."
        },
        {
          "const": "edit_entry",
          "description": "Edit an existing goal activity entry. Required args: update_id and at least one of title, current_state, description, effective_at. Keep the entry concise and user-facing, saying what happened and, when applicable, what the result was."
        },
        {
          "const": "delete_entry",
          "description": "Delete an existing goal progress entry. Required args: update_id."
        },
        {
          "const": "set_status",
          "description": "Set the goal lifecycle to active or completed. Required args: goal_id, status, reason. Reason must concisely explain why the lifecycle changed. Use active only to reopen the existing completed goal when the user explicitly restarts the responsibility; never create a replacement goal."
        }
      ],
      "type": "string"
    },
    "category": {
      "description": "For user goals, selects the coaching guide linked from the goal's GOAL.md.",
      "enum": [
        "health",
        "relationships",
        "money",
        "career",
        "interests",
        "productivity",
        "something_else"
      ],
      "type": "string"
    },
    "current_state": {
      "description": "The one-line user-facing state. For goal metadata of every type, write one short pulse from the newest evidence that states the single most useful current or forward-looking status: a result, progress marker, specific wait, blocker, monitored condition, or scheduled event. Do not claim work is currently in progress, append a generic next step, or restate the title or description. For add_entry or edit_entry, state the activity's main outcome.",
      "type": "string"
    },
    "description": {
      "description": "For create or update, write two or three natural, user-facing sentences that explain the goal at a high level. Put detailed progress and state changes in entries instead. For add_entry or edit_entry, write one concise, human-friendly sentence about what happened and, when applicable, what the result was.",
      "type": "string"
    },
    "effective_at": {
      "type": "string"
    },
    "emoji": {
      "type": "string"
    },
    "goal_id": {
      "type": "string"
    },
    "goal_kind": {
      "description": "outcome = result to achieve. behavior = action pattern to adopt. learning = skill to acquire (spaced study, user goals only). habit = recurring practice. maintenance = hold a standard. recovery = return from a setback. identity = who the user wants to become. exploratory = open-ended discovery.",
      "enum": [
        "outcome",
        "behavior",
        "learning",
        "habit",
        "maintenance",
        "recovery",
        "identity",
        "exploratory"
      ],
      "type": "string"
    },
    "limit": {
      "maximum": 100,
      "minimum": 1,
      "type": "integer"
    },
    "parent_goal_id": {
      "description": "The parent must be a top-level goal.",
      "type": "string"
    },
    "pushable": {
      "description": "For a user-goal update, set false when the user says to stop proactive brief pushes (reads still show briefs in the Goals tab).",
      "type": "boolean"
    },
    "query": {
      "description": "Terms to match against goal id, title, current_state, and description. Required for search.",
      "minLength": 2,
      "type": "string"
    },
    "reason": {
      "description": "Required for set_status. Concise user-facing explanation of why the lifecycle changed.",
      "minLength": 1,
      "type": "string"
    },
    "status": {
      "description": "The complete model-facing lifecycle for goals: active means the responsibility remains open, completed means it ended.",
      "enum": [
        "active",
        "completed"
      ],
      "type": "string"
    },
    "title": {
      "description": "Concise user-facing noun phrase naming the goal itself, not an instruction. Avoid generic leading verbs like `Track ...`; use concrete domain wording (`Wimbledon daily analysis`, `Childcare coordination`). Current activity and status go in current_state.",
      "type": "string"
    },
    "update_id": {
      "type": "string"
    },
    "value_alignment": {
      "type": "string"
    }
  },
  "required": [
    "action"
  ],
  "type": "object"
}
```

